In .NET MAUI Shell, you can't directly cancel Shell navigation, but you can combine a few techniques:

### 1. Custom "Cancel" back button

In your `EditProductPage.xaml`:

```xml
<ContentPage xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/dotnet/2021/maui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2009/xaml"
             x:Class="MyApp.EditProductPage"
             Shell.BackButtonBehavior="{StaticResource CancelBackButton}">

    <ContentPage.Resources>
        <BackButtonBehavior x:Key="CancelBackButton"
                            TextOverride="Cancel"
                            Command="{Binding GoBackCommand}" />
    </ContentPage.Resources>

    <!-- your form here -->
</ContentPage>
```

This replaces the default back arrow with a "Cancel" text button and routes taps through your command.

### 2. Confirmation logic in your ViewModel

```csharp
public partial class EditProductViewModel : ObservableObject
{
    [ObservableProperty]
    private bool _hasUnsavedChanges;

    [RelayCommand]
    private async Task GoBack()
    {
        if (HasUnsavedChanges)
        {
            bool leave = await Shell.Current.DisplayAlert(
                "Unsaved Changes",
                "You have unsaved changes. Discard and go back?",
                "Discard", "Stay");

            if (!leave)
                return; // cancel navigation
        }

        await Shell.Current.GoToAsync("..");
    }
}
```

### 3. Intercept the hardware/software back button

The `BackButtonBehavior` only handles the **Shell toolbar** button. To also catch the **Android hardware/gesture back** and the **system back** on other platforms, override `OnBackButtonPressed` in your code-behind:

```csharp
public partial class EditProductPage : ContentPage
{
    public EditProductPage(EditProductViewModel vm)
    {
        InitializeComponent();
        BindingContext = vm;
    }

    protected override bool OnBackButtonPressed()
    {
        var vm = (EditProductViewModel)BindingContext;

        if (!vm.HasUnsavedChanges)
            return false; // allow default back navigation

        // Fire-and-forget the async confirmation dialog
        Dispatcher.Dispatch(async () =>
        {
            await vm.GoBackCommand.ExecuteAsync(null);
        });

        return true; // suppress default navigation for now
    }
}
```

**Key points:**
- `BackButtonBehavior` handles the Shell chrome back button and lets you customize its text/icon.
- `OnBackButtonPressed()` returning `true` suppresses the system back gesture.
- The actual navigation (`GoToAsync("..")`) only fires after the user confirms in the dialog.
- Set `HasUnsavedChanges` whenever a form field changes (e.g., via property setters or `Entry.TextChanged`).
